^{:go/end 364} (go/func tzset "tzset takes a timezone string like the one found in the TZ environment\nvariable, the time of the last time zone transition expressed as seconds\nsince January 1, 1970 00:00:00 UTC, and a time expressed the same way.\nWe call this a tzset string since in C the function tzset reads TZ.\nThe return values are as for lookup, plus ok which reports whether the\nparse succeeded.\n" [^string s ^int64 lastTxSec ^int64 sec] :results [^string name ^int offset ^int64 start ^int64 end ^bool isDST ^bool ok]
